    "sha": "f69e56bc1c43ca2bebd4d733bce1afc8de8f58b9"
   },
   "harm": "Configuring maxfeerate as a node-wide option instead of wallet-only bleeds wallet settings into node RPCs and removes useful mempool RPC options",
   "hash": "197c0e414fe48ea7",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-18T03:26:40+00:00",
     "blocking": true,
     "by": "run:20260918-0314",
     "cause": "r:1832875650",
     "status": "resolved"
    }
   ],
   "id": "r:1832875650",
   "kind": "approach",
   "pin": null,
   "quote": "I don't think that wallet configurations should bleed into how the node RPCs function. Instead, the interaction there should be for wallet to pass it as a param to BroadcastTransaction when the it submits a tx to the node.",
   "settled_by": {
    "at": "2024-01-25",
    "by": "ismaelsadeeq",
    "id": "c:1911091517",
    "quote": "Made maxfeerate wallet option"
   },
   "status": "resolved",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/29278#pullrequestreview-1832875650"
  },
  {
   "association": "MEMBER",
   "at": "2024-01-29",
   "author": "josibake",
   "author_replies": [
    "rc:1472785028",
    "rc:1472858661",
    "rc:1477791006"
   ],
   "blocking": false,
   "fix": {
    "at": null,
    "sha": "f69e56bc1c43ca2bebd4d733bce1afc8de8f58b9"
   },
   "harm": "Removing the check for max_fee resulting in feerate below relayMinFee permits users to set unworkable maxtxfee values without startup warnings",
   "hash": "e229cf40b95c5773",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-18T03:26:40+00:00",
     "blocking": false,
     "by": "run:20260918-0314",
     "cause": "rc:1469372132",
     "status": "resolved"
    }
   ],
   "id": "rc:1469372132",
   "kind": "correctness",
   "pin": null,
   "quote": "I don't think we should remove this check for setting a max_fee that results in fee rates less than the relayMinFee.",
   "settled_by": {
    "at": "2024-02-05",
    "by": "ismaelsadeeq",
    "id": "rc:1477791006",
    "quote": "I agree with @josibake suggestion and added a commit that performs the same check in wallet initialization as before."
   },
   "status": "resolved",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/29278#discussion_r1469372132"
  },
  {
   "association": "MEMBER",
   "at": "2024-01-31",
   "author": "murchandamus",
   "author_replies": [
    "rc:1477810958"
   ],
   "blocking": false,
   "fix": {
    "at": null,
    "sha": "f69e56bc1c43ca2bebd4d733bce1afc8de8f58b9"
   },
   "harm": "Replacing descriptive error messages with a generic string obscures which limit (maxtxfee or maxfeerate) was hit",
   "hash": "e7336f2a3970490a",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-18T03:26:40+00:00",
     "blocking": false,
     "by": "run:20260918-0314",
     "cause": "rc:1473275731",
     "status": "resolved"
    }
   ],
   "id": "rc:1473275731",
   "kind": "interface",
   "pin": null,
   "quote": "It isn\u2019t clear to me why we would first ship a less descriptive new error message in this PR and then immediately fix it in a follow-up.",
   "settled_by": {
    "at": "2024-02-05",
    "by": "ismaelsadeeq",
    "id": "rc:1477810958",
    "quote": "However I agree with your comment, I have now added a commit that also checks the fee rate limit in BroadcastTransaction, and changed how sendrawtransaction is implemented, and updated the MAX_FEE_EXCEEDED transaction error type message."
   },
   "status": "resolved",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/29278#discussion_r1473275731"
  },
  {
   "association": "MEMBER",
   "at": "2026-08-27",
   "author": "polespinasa",
   "author_replies": [
    "c:5655683492"
   ],
   "blocking": true,
   "fix": {
    "at": null,
    "sha": "f69e56bc1c43ca2bebd4d733bce1afc8de8f58b9"
   },
   "harm": "sendall ignores bump fees for unconfirmed inputs when evaluating maxfeerate, causing transaction creation to succeed while broadcast fails silently",
   "hash": "cc8d403ec28cad1e",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-18T03:26:40+00:00",
     "blocking": true,
     "by": "run:20260918-0314",
     "cause": "c:5441203296",
     "status": "resolved"
    }
   ],
   "id": "c:5441203296",
   "kind": "correctness",
   "pin": null,
   "quote": "sendall's creation-time -maxfeerate check ignores bump fees for unconfirmed inputs, while the broadcast-time check in BroadcastTransaction includes them. When fee_rate is set exactly equal to -maxfeerate and the wallet spends unconfirmed inputs with positive bump fees, the creation check passes... but the broadcast check fails",
   "settled_by": {
    "at": "2026-09-15",
    "by": "polespinasa",
    "id": "r:5213483629",
    "quote": "ACK f69e56bc1c43ca2bebd4d733bce1afc8de8f58b9"
   },
   "status": "resolved",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/29278#issuecomment-5441203296"
  }
 ],
